# ResearchData/.gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: the *description* of an experiment is versioned, the *bytes* are not.
# Markdown, YAML, CSV and JSON stay in git. Captures, spectrograms and weights do not.

# Raw captures and array dumps ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.iq
*.cf32
*.cs16
*.sigmf-data
*.bin
*.dat
*.wav
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.mat

# Rendered spectrograms ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.webp

# Archives -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# Dataset scan caches ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cache

# Note: *.txt is deliberately NOT ignored. YOLO label files are small, diffable and cannot be regenerated, so they are
# versioned along with the dataset card. Reviewer notes, capture logs and similar text belong in git for the same reason.

# Training outputs (also ignored by the repo-root .gitignore, repeated here so this folder is self-describing) --------
runs/

# Keep placeholder images that document a format, if you ever add one --------------------------------------------------
!docs/**/*.png
